:0.9,"rationale":"Retailers import finished goods and consumer products; terminating the tariffs would affect pricing and supply-chain costs."},{"industry":"agriculture","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"Agricultural exporters face retaliatory tariffs from trading partners; ending the emergency could reduce trade tensions affecting farm exports."},{"industry":"tech","confidence":0.75,"rationale":"Technology companies import hardware, semiconductors, and components; tariff removal would affect production costs and supply chains."},{"industry":"transport","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Shipping and logistics firms handle import volumes; changes in tariff policy affect freight demand and cross-border trade flows."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"5ee9a0d4a8f80755b36569ca","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:47:56.088Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoes":"This joint resolution would end the national emergency declared by President Donald J. Trump on April 2, 2025, which imposed a 10% tariff on most imports to the United States and additional duties on specified trading partners.","whoItTouches":"Anyone who buys imported goods, and people who make goods here.","everydayEffect":"If it passed, the change would show up in prices, and what is made where. Nothing has changed yet. Most bills never become law.","confidence":"crs-summary","source":"Reworded from the official summary. Staff at the Congressional Research Service wrote that summary. It is public domain, and the full text of it is further down this page.","titleInPlainWords":null},"overlaps":[{"billId":"119-sjres-49","bioguideId":"W000800","cycle":2026,"score":0.017472402548741228,"matches":[{"industry":"tech","donorAmount":5000,"donorShare":0.06532474826781631,"billConfidence":0.75,"contribution":0.011805677397798127},{"industry":"retail-consumer","donorAmount":2000,"donorShare":0.026129899307126527,"billConfidence":0.9,"contribution":0.005666725150943102}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(